@startuml
skinparam actorStyle awesome
autonumber

actor "Industrial PC (Hardware)" as HW
participant "fs-ingest-daemon" as HUNT
database "config.json" as CFG
database "SQLite (hunt.db)" as DB
participant "Cloud API" as API

== 1. Initialization & Identity Discovery ==
HUNT -> HW : Query MAC Address & CPU Serial (Non-Admin)
return Hardware Signals
HUNT -> HUNT : Generate SHA-256 Hardware Hash (DeviceID)

== 2. Equipment Registration (First-Time Only) ==
HUNT -> CFG : Check for AuthToken
CFG --> HUNT : AuthToken is Empty

HUNT -> API : POST /register {DeviceID, OS, Hostname, HW_Info}
note right: Ensures the cloud knows this specific IPC
API -> API : Validate/Create Equipment Record
return 201 Created {AuthToken, CloudConfig}

HUNT -> CFG : Update DeviceID & Save AuthToken
HUNT -> HUNT : Lock Identity (Immutable)

== 3. File Watcher & Detection ==
HW -> HUNT : File System Event (New Image)
HUNT -> HUNT : Debounce (Wait for write to finish)
HUNT -> DB : Insert Record (Status: PENDING)

== 4. Managed Ingestion Handshake ==
loop Every IngestCheckInterval
    HUNT -> DB : Get PENDING Files
    DB --> HUNT : List of Files

    HUNT -> API : POST /ingest {DeviceID, AuthToken, FileMetadata}
    note right: Handshake for S3 Upload URL
    API --> HUNT : 200 OK {HandshakeID, UploadURL}

    HUNT -> API : PUT Binary to UploadURL (S3)
    return 200 OK (Transfer Success)

    HUNT -> API : POST /confirm {HandshakeID, Status: SUCCESS}
    return 200 OK

    HUNT -> DB : Update Status to UPLOADED
end
@enduml